WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.080
A drop of pond water can look completely clear.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.700
But tiny living things in that drop, an onion and you are all made of cells.

3
00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:15.763
A cell is the smallest unit that can carry out the processes of life.

4
00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.063
The cell theory has three parts.

5
00:00:18.943 --> 00:00:21.203
All living things are made of one or more cells.

6
00:00:22.123 --> 00:00:23.923
The cell is the basic unit of life.

7
00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:27.063
All cells come from cells that already exist.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:30.277
Some organisms are just one cell.

9
00:00:31.157 --> 00:00:32.157
They are unicellular.

10
00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:35.277
A Paramecium in pond water is one cell.

11
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:39.217
You and an oak tree are multicellular, made of many cells.

12
00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:41.857
Tiny does not always mean one cell.

13
00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:44.717
Some tiny pond animals have many cells.

14
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:50.540
In science, a theory is a well-tested explanation backed by a great deal of

15
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.160
evidence. The cell theory grew as better microscopes gave new evidence.

16
00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.560
Scientists found cells in many plants and animals.

17
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.700
Some once thought new cells formed from clear fluid.

18
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.060
More observations showed that new cells form when a cell divides.

19
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.500
The theory dropped the wrong idea and kept the rest.

20
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.920
Most cells are too small to see without help.

21
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.360
Your eye can make out details down to about 100 micrometres.

22
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.540
A microscope uses lenses to make small things look larger.

23
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.880
Magnification tells us how many times larger the image looks.

24
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:28.823
Seeing fine detail matters too.

25
00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:34.123
The best light microscopes show details down to about 0.2 micrometres.

26
00:01:35.043 --> 00:01:37.083
A school microscope shows most whole cells.

27
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.843
Electron microscopes use electrons instead of light.

28
00:01:41.723 --> 00:01:44.743
They showed cell parts too small for ordinary light microscopes.

29
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:50.687
Cells differ in shape and size, depending on their job and the organism they belong

30
00:01:50.687 --> 00:01:54.787
to. A red blood cell is a disc, pressed in on both faces.

31
00:01:55.727 --> 00:01:57.687
A nerve cell can have long, thin branches.
